-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",6,{
[161]="70030370\n1\tAid Gísling\030Aid Langar\030Aid Gísil\tGísil and Gísling can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. Langar can be found in west Garsfeld. Gísil wants you to aid him and the people of Garsfeld with final tasks before the townsfolk evacuate to Snowbourn.\n2\tTalk to Gísil\tGísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. You should return to Gísil and let him know that you have completed his tasks.\n",
[162]="7001757B\n1\tDefeat Pukhal\tPukhal can be found south and then west of Anazârmekhem in the north-western reaches of the Flaming Deeps. Garnyd has tasked you with killing the Orc Pukhal.\n2\tTalk to Garnyd at Anazârmekhem\tGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem, in the northern reaches of the Flaming Deeps. You should return to Garnyd with news of your success.\n",
[163]="70016719\n1\tCollect pieces of scaffold (total: 8)\tPieces of scaffold can be found in the tunnels east of Hadâd-mezer and Bhraf-ru, both south of Anazârmekhem. You should collect pieces of scaffold for the repairs going on beneath the Cross-roads of Ash.\n2\tBring the pieces of scaffold to Gapi at Anazârmekhem\tGapi is at Anazârmekhem, located to the north-west of Hadâd-mezer. You should bring the scaffold-pieces you gathered to Gapi.\n",
[164]="70057F5E\n1\tDispose of half-emptied bottles in the High Hall (total: 10)\030Remove noisy revellers from the High Hall (total: 6)\tHalf-emptied bottles and noisy revellers can be found in the High Hall in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Ioreth has tasked you with disposing of half-emptied bottles of ale and wine and removing noisy revellers from the High Hall.\n2\tTalk to Ioreth\tIoreth can be found in the High Hall in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have disposed of half-emptied bottles and removed noisy revellers from the High Hall. You should return to Ioreth.\n",
[165]="7006566B\n1\tFind the food stall run by Haradrim\tAccording to Othor, there is a food stall run by Haradrim towards the southern end of West Pelargir. You should find it.\n2\tTalk to Jódha\tYou have found the food stall in West Pelargir. You should talk to Jódha to order food.\n3\tWait for Jódha to finish your order\tYou have found the food stall in West Pelargir and given your order. You should wait for Jódha to finish cooking.\n4\tTalk to Jódha\tJódha has finished cooking your food. You should talk to her at her food stall in West Pelargir.\n5\tReturn to Othor near the West Pelargir gates\tYou have retrieved the food for Othor, Nasar, and the other Corsairs. You should return to them near the West Pelargir gates.\n6\tTalk to Nasar\tNasar waits near the West Pelargir gates. He seems to want to talk to you.\n",
[166]="70068322\n1\tPick up the hammer\tThe rogue was tasked with delivering this hammer to the leader of Halrax, Ithurga.\n2\tBring the weapon to Ithurga in Halrax\tYou have successfully removed the strange hammer from the stone. According to the man, you should deliver the item to Ithurga. Ithurga can be found in Halrax.\n",
[167]="7000A2A4\n1\tCollect Choice Cut of Bear-meat (total: 8)\tBears roam the hills of Tyrn Fornech and can especially be found at Nan Orngon, east of Ost Forod. Parr Chopley has asked you to bring him choice cuts of bear-meat from the bears that roam Tyrn Fornech.\n2\tBring choice cuts of bear-meat to Parr Chopley\tParr Chopley is in the old watch-post of Ost Forod, in the hills of Tyrn Fornech, west of Nan Orngon. You have collected several choice cuts of bear-meat and should bring them to Parr Chopley.\n",
[168]="70066CDB\n1\tFind the cursed child\tGerech the Addled has asked you to help with a cursed child who seems to be a sign for imminent doom to Anfalas. The cursed child can be found in the bluffs to the south-west.\n2\tScare the huntsman away\tThe Huntsman refuses to give up the cursed child. You should intimidate them and scare them away.\n3\tTalk to Endela\tThe Huntsman has been scared away. You should reason with the cursed child.\n4\tConfront Gerech the Addled\tEndela has revealed to you the terrible treatment she suffered. You should confront Gerech. Gerech the Addled can be found in Barad Faen.\n5\tTalk to Endela\tGerech forced your hand and has been defeated. You should tell Endela she is free. Endela can be found in the bluffs to the south-west.\n",
[169]="70061F74\n1\tReturn the stolen necklace\tArnail has asked you to return a stolen necklace to a barrow near Dol Ernil. Dol Ernil is in north-western Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Nan Mabli\tYou should let Nan Mabli know that you have returned the stolen necklace to the barrows. Nan Mabli is near the barrows south of Dol Ernil.\n",
[170]="70041173\n1\tDefeat the Dead in Tarlang's Crown (total: 8)\tThe Dead can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown. You have encountered the Dead and should defeat them to free the Crown of their terror.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Dead in Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[171]="7003022F\n1\tDefeat vicious Fangorn Huorns (total: 10)\tVicious Fangorn Huorns encircle the wounded man, threatening to kill him or any creature who wander into this part of the forest. You should defeat the enraged Huorns so that they may no longer threaten the wounded man.\n2\tReturn to Léofmar\tLéofmar is curled up by a log in the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should return to Léofmar now that this part of the forest is safer from the threatening Huorns.\n",
[172]="70030433\n1\tBehead Orcs in the south camp (total: 8)\030Collect spears from Orcs in Ash Durub or Ufum-mau (total: 8)\tOrcs and their heads can be found in the camps of Ufum-mau and Ash Durub, located to the south-west and west of Walstow, respectively.\n2\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow.\n",
[173]="7006906C\n1\tDefeat Corsair deck-hands (total: 8)\030Defeat Corsair look-outs (total: 10)\030Defeat Corsair brutes (total: 3)\tTake the fight to Ghasaphâr and his Corsairs. Root them out of their settlement in Kan Skûrja on the Cape of Umbar.\n2\tDefeat the Corsair Captain Ghasaphâr\tDefeat the Corsair Captain Ghasaphâr.\n",
[174]="70034245\n1\tDefeat Orc Warg-riders in the Whitshaws (total: 10)\tWarg-riders can be found roaming the plains of the Whitshaws. You should defeat Warg-riders in the Whitshaws.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of Warg-riders in the Whitshaws, but the forces of Isengard will soon return.\n",
[175]="70066856\n1\tFind Thendor, Glamion, and Randis at the Hill of Erech\tThendor, Glamion, and Randis can be found at the Hill of Erech, to the west of Lancrath in the Blackroot Vale. Berthalend has asked you to find Thendor, Glamion, and Randis before they endanger themselves at the Hill of Erech.\n2\tTalk to Thendor at the Hill of Erech\030Talk to Glamion at the Hill of Erech\tThendor and Glamion can be found at the foot of the Hill of Erech near Lancrath, in the Blackroot Vale. You have found Thendor and Glamion, but Randis does not appear to be with them. You should talk to Thendor and Glamion.\n3\tFind Randis at the Hill of Erech\tRandis can be found at the Hill of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale. Thendor and Glamion believe Randis is trying to fulfil her dare: to touch the Stone of Erech. You should find Randis.\n4\tTalk to Randis at the Hill of Erech\tRandis can be found at the Stone of Erech, in the Blackroot Vale. You have found Randis near the Stone of Erech, but she is clearly uneasy. You should talk to Randis.\n5\tTalk to Berthalend\tBerthalend can be found in Lancrath, in the Blackroot Vale. You have convinced Randis, Thendor, and Glamion to return to Lancrath. You should talk to Berthalend.\n",
[176]="7004300C\n1\tTalk to Spalvi in the narrow pass\tBingo's new friend Spalvi is in the narrow pass in the Misty Mountains north of Glóin's camp, on the way to the Northern Bruinen Source.\n2\tTalk to Spalvi in the narrow pass and travel with him to Helegrod\tSpalvi is in the narrow pass north of Glóin's camp, in the Misty Mountains. Spalvi and his brothers were attacked by Corcur nomads in the Misty Mountains, and the dwarf was left for dead and his valuables stolen. Bingo has volunteered to track the Corcur nomads to Helegrod to reclaim Spalvi's treasure, and the dwarf is waiting to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Glóin at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell\tGlóin is at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell. Spalvi has revealed himself to be a Dourhand, and he has hobbitnapped Bingo! You know you will need a plan if you are to rescue the hobbit.\n",
[177]="7001CEF4\n1\tSummon and defeat the Dourstocks Lair-spinner\tThe Dourstocks Lair-spinner can be found in the Dreadweaver's Lair. You should go to the spider-lair and face the Lair-spinner.\n2\tTalk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn\tFernachar is in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks. You should return to Fernachar with word of your triumph against the Dourstocks Lair-spinner.\n",
[178]="700379DD\n1\tFind Húnbrit, who rode east and south\030Find Winmar, who rode north\030Find Ordgar, who rode north-west\030Find Cúthsig, who rode west\030(Assist Húnbrit)\030(Assist Gandalf)\tThe four scouts rode out west, north-west, north-east, and south-east from Grimslade. You should search for and assist the four scouts sent out by Hildith to search for Grimbold.\n2\tReturn to Hildith\tHildith can be found in the Mead Hall of Grimslade in the Westfold. You should return to Hildith.\n",
[179]="7000E837\n1\tVisit Barachen's Camp\tBegin your patrol at Barachen's Camp, which can be found in the hills South of the road as it runs East from the Last Bridge.\n2\tScout the Stone-trolls' Glade\tFind the glade occupied by a set of three petrified Stone-trolls. It lies somewhere in the hills North-east of Barachen's camp.\n3\tScout the ruins of Drauglad\tScout the ruins of Drauglad, south-east of the Stone-troll's Glade.\n4\tScout the Ford of Bruinen\tScout the Ford of Bruinen, which lies South-east of the ruins of Drauglad.\n5\tTalk to Handarod\tReport to Handarod and tell him the results of your patrol in the Western Trollshaws.\n",
[180]="70047AE5\n1\tEnter the Towers of the Teeth\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should weaken support beams in the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tWeaken support beams (total: 10)\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should weaken support beams in the Towers of the Teeth.\n3\tCompleted\tWeakened many support beams in the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
[181]="7000A172\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House, far to the east within the Trollshaws. Ferrod has asked you to speak with Aragorn, telling you that with dedication, sticking to the roads, and travelling only by day, you can safely reach Rivendell.\n",
[182]="7002F890\n1\tHelp escort Runald's family to safety\tRunald and his family await at the southern entrance to the village of Elthengels. Runald has asked you to help escort his family safely along the first section of their journey west.\n2\tThank Ofrith at the trader's outpost for his help\tOfrith can be found within the trader's outpost, west along the road from Elthengels. Runald has made it safely to the trader's outpost and has taken the road south. He has asked you to give his thanks to Ofrith for his support.\n",
[183]="70047ADF\n1\tHide traps in rubble piles (quantity: see journal)\tGood places to hide traps can be found within the Towers of the Teeth. You should hide traps in rubble piles within the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tReturn to Thurindol\tYou should return to Thurindol, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[184]="7002CDEC\n1\tHelp Stanric take back Stangard\tStanric is in the lock-house. You should free Stanric from his bonds.\n2\tTalk to Stanric\tStanric is now in the Mead Hall, alone, in his proper place. You should speak with Stanric once more.\n",
[185]="700430A1\n1\tDefeat Dourhands at the fortress of Gabilazan (total: 12)\tDourhands can be found in the fortress of Gabilazan, in the High Crag of the Misty Mountains. Glóin believes you can learn where the Dourhands are holding Bingo Boffin if you attack them at the fortress of Gabilazan.\n2\tFind the courtyard in the southern reaches of Gabilazan\tYou heard some shouting from the southern reaches of Gabilazan. Is that where Bingo is being held captive?\n3\tSearch the slopes just north of Gabilazan for any sign of Bingo's escape\tBingo was being held in a cage in Gabilazan, but somehow he has managed to escape! You should search the slopes north of Gabilazan for any sign of Bingo's escape.\n4\tTalk to Spalvi Dourhand by the hole in the mountain\tSpalvi Dourhand stands by a deep, dark hole in the mountain, just north of Gabilazan. What story does HE have to tell?\n5\tCollect bundles of food from Gabilazan (total: 4)\030Collect water-bottles from Dourhands in Gabilazan (total: 6)\tSpalvi Dourhand has had a change of heart, and wishes to help you rescue Bingo. Spalvi helped free Bingo from Gabilazan, but the hobbit fell down a hole during the escape. The Dourhand now wants to help you save Bingo, and thinks you can retrieve bundles of food and bottles of water from Gabilazan that you can drop down the hole to Bingo, if the hobbit survived the fall.\n6\tDrop the supplies from Gabilazan down the deep, dark hole\tSpalvi Dourhand is standing next to a deep, dark hole just north of Gabilazan. You have collected supplies for Bingo, and should drop them down the hole to him, in case the hobbit survived the fall.\n7\tTalk to Spalvi Dourhand by the deep, dark hole\tSpalvi Dourhand is standing by the deep, dark hole just north of Gabilazan, in the Misty Mountains.\n",
[186]="70000046\n1\tTalk to Leofwenna\tThe arch leading from the ruins lies to the west. Leofwenna has asked you to escort her to the arch leading out of the ruins and to freedom. She is in the area east beyond the first of the goblin camps south-east of The Forsaken Inn.\n2\tTalk to Gadaric Munce\tGadaric Munce is at The Forsaken Inn, north-west of the ruins. Leofwenna suggested you seek Gadaric Munce, and that he would reward you for assisting her.\n",
[187]="7000E8FC\n1\tCollect Moor-boar Beer from the Prancing Pony\tMoor-boar Beer can be found in The Prancing Pony of Bree-town. You should appeal to Barliman Butterbur for a sample of some Moor-boar Beer.\n2\tBring the Moor-boar Beer to Lófi\tThe Prancing Pony Inn is in the town of Bree in Bree-land, far to the south of Forochel. Lófi is at Zigilgund in Forochel, far to the north of Bree-land. Lófi has told you his sad tale, that he is without the beer he needs to complete the Inn League Challenge. He asked if you could bring him the beer he needs, \"Moor-boar Beer,\" which can only be found at The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree.\n",
[188]="70055077\n1\tRetrieve arrows from slain merrevail (total: 12)\tArrows can be found embedded in slain merrevail in the Circle of Death and the Circle of Despair. Echil has asked you to retrieve spent arrows from slain merrevail, so his men might be better prepared for the battles ahead.\n2\tDeliver the stained arrows to Echil in the Circle of Death\tEchil can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul. You have retrieved many arrows from slain merrevail and should now deliver them to Echil.\n",
[189]="7006EB92\n1\tSpeak with Razâl when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Razâl outside the tower in Kûr Anzar when you are ready.\n2\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh.\n",
[190]="70040430\n1\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad. Malthellam has asked you to rally with Gúrion at the Hill of Erech in hopes of exposing the identity of the strange Man from Tarlang's Crown.\n2\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad in Blackroot Vale. You encountered Azruthor, a Black Númenórean sorcerer and one of the Heirs of Castamir. His grim task came to fruition, but he fled back to Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[191]="700216E4\n1\tCollect fake Moor-boar Beer from The Floating Log\tThe Floating Log is in Frogmorton in the Shire. You should get a pint of Toad's Tongue Ale from Ponto Hopsbloom, the tavern keep at The Floating Log.\n2\tBring the fake Moor-boar Beer to Lófi in Forochel\tLófi is at Zigilgund in Forochel, far to the frozen north. You should bring the fake Moor-boar Beer, which is actually Toad's Tongue Ale in disguise, to Lófi before it is too late.\n",
[192]="70069073\n1\tFind and collect the treasure cache\030Defeat Corsairs (total: 12)\tCorsairs have beaten you to the treasure! Defeat the Corsairs and claim the treasure cache for the free peoples of Umbar.\n2\tDefeat Captain Shêndi Grey-eye\tFind and defeat Captain Shêndi Grey-eye\n",
})
